# keybind.keys -- exercises step 4 of build/plans/isocline.rst: the
# ic_bind_key()/ic_unbind_key() keybinding mechanism and the
# ic_history_count()/ic_history_get() public accessors.  Driven
# through the jig's test bindings on ctrl-G, ctrl-V and ctrl-X; see
# jig_dismiss_action/jig_check_suppressed_action/jig_history_dump_action
# in jig.c.
#
# Part 1 (keybindings): ctrl-G is hardwired by isocline to cancel and
# clear the input outright.  "ab" surviving the ctrl-G below proves a
# bound action overrides that built-in behavior completely.  The
# suppression flag it sets (ic_keyaction_dismiss_completions) is then
# observed still set (ctrl-V), cleared by the next word boundary (a
# space), and observed cleared (ctrl-V again).
i 2
+ ab
k C-G
k C-V
k SPACE
k C-V
k ENTER
w 20
#
# Part 2 (history accessors): "ab " is now the one completed entry in
# the history.  Typing "cd" on this next line (without pressing
# ENTER) leaves a fresh, still-blank placeholder entry live ahead of
# it, so ic_history_count()/ic_history_get() report two entries,
# most-recent first: index 0 is that blank placeholder, index 1 is
# "ab ".
+ cd
k C-X
w 20
q
